%T A401422 4,9,2,4,4,4,2,8,2,6,6,4,2,8,3,6,4,6,2,4,4,4,4,4,2,12,2,4,6,3,4,8,2,6,
%U A401422 4,8,2,6,2,4,6,6,4,8,2,8,4,4,2,12,4,4,4,4,2,12
%N A401422 The number of terms in A138302 that divide the smallest coreful infinitary divisor of n.
%H A401422 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A401422/b401422.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A401422 a(n) = A353898(A365296(n)).
%F A401422 Multiplicative with a(p^e) = A001511(e) + 1 = A007814(e) + 2.
%F A401422 a(n) >= 2 for n >= 2, with equality if and only if n is a prime power with an odd exponent (A246551).
%F A401422 a(n) = 3 if and only if n is a square of a term in A246551, i.e., a prime power with an even exponent that is not a multiple of 4.
%F A401422 a(n) >= A034444(n), with equality if and only if n is an exponentially odd number (A268335).
%t A401422 f[p_, e_] := IntegerExponent[e, 2] + 2; a[1] = 1; a[n_] := Times @@ f @@@ FactorInteger[n]; Array[a, 90]
%o A401422 (PARI) a(n) = vecprod(apply(x -> valuation(x, 2) + 2, factor(n)[, 2]));
%Y A401422 Cf. A001511, A007814, A034444, A138302, A246551, A268335, A353898, A365296, A392447.
%K A401422 nonn,mult,easy,new
%O A401422 1,2
%A A401422 _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 24 2026
